# Google Maps Platform API key — used server-side only, never sent to the browser.
#
# Powers three serverless functions:
#   /api/drivetimes  → Distance Matrix API  (traffic-aware drive times)
#   /api/places      → Places API           (discover nearby centers / airports)
#   /api/geocode     → Geocoding API         (search-to-add a site by address)
#   /api/streetview  → Street View Static API + Maps Static API (location image)
# Enable "Distance Matrix API", "Places API", "Geocoding API",
# "Street View Static API", and "Maps Static API" on the key.
#
# Production (Vercel): set this in
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables  (add to all environments),
#   then redeploy.
#
# Local testing: copy this file to `.env` and run `vercel dev` (plain
# `vite dev` does not run the /api function).
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# AirportDB.io token — server-side only, used by /api/airport to look up an
# airport by ICAO code (official name, exact coordinates, IATA code, runways).
# Free token from https://airportdb.io/ . Optional: without it, the airport
# "Look up ICAO" button returns a clear "add a token" message.
AIRPORTDB_API_TOKEN=
